   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Mount Kisco; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8161",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8161-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-z-3, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S8161\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to the\nimposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Mount Kisco; and\nproviding for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo authorize the Village of Mount Kisco to enact a room occupancy tax\nnot to exceed 3%.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThe tax law is amended to add a new section 1202-z3, to authorize the\nVillage of Mount Kisco to enact such a tax.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Village of Mount Kisco seeks the authority to impose a 3% daily\nroom tax on any room in a hotel, motel, or similar place. This tax is\nintended to raise revenues to support municipal expenses. The tax has\nbeen successful in the nearby cities of New Rochelle, Rye, and White\nPlains. Chapter 381 of the Laws of 2010 grants similar authority to\nthe Village of Rye Brook, also in Westchester County.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State, but increased revenue for the Village of Mount\nKisco.\n\n IMPACT ON REGULATION OF BUSINESSES AND INDIVIDUALS :\n\nNo additional regulations; the tax is calculated like a sales tax and\nis remitted directly to the town.\n\n EFFECT ON FINES, TERMS OF IMPRISONMENT OR OTHER PENAL SANCTIONS :\n\nNone\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed September 1, 2019.\n",
